<title>PORTUGAL: Improved margins, commissions help BCP net.</title>
<headline>Improved margins, commissions help BCP net.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Improved margins, growth in commissions, trading gains and a reduction in costs helped boost first half profits of Portugal's biggest private bank Banco Comercial Portugues, a statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The sustained increase in the financial margin, a significant growth in commissions and a reduction in costs were the main reasons for the increase in BCP's net results,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>BCP said it raised first half net consolidated profits by 21 percent to 13.12 billion escudos ($72 million).</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
